{
  "about": "r9-17 / r8-13: the incoming-funds scan as one rule. `plans`: TrustScanFacts -> IncomingScanPlan (incoming_scan::scan_plan; wasm incomingScanPlan, uniffi incoming_scan_plan). `windows`: IncomingScanWindowsAsk -> IncomingScanWindows (scan_windows; incomingScanWindows / incoming_scan_windows). `cadence` (r10): (visible, quiet_scans) -> next scan in ms (next_scan_ms; incomingNextScanMs / incoming_next_scan_ms) — a back-off while nothing arrives. `cadence_steps` (r10): the activity_feed machine's cadence, step by step — each step is one thing that happens (`do`), at `at` seconds after the start, on a page shown unless `visible` is false; `expect` says whether the step issued a scan (ScanIncomingTransfers) and a store read (ReadTxStore), how many renders it asked for, and the timer it armed (`armed`: the new next_scan.after_ms, or null when the timer did not move). `do`: account_switched, presence:<change> (presence_changed), scan_due (the current next_scan.seq), scan_due_stale (the seq before it), interacting_on / interacting_off (interacting {on}), scan_answer (SyncCompleted {new_count}), store_answer (every outstanding ReadTxStore answered with no records). Replayed by rust/crates/vela-core/tests/app_incoming_scan.rs; every shell replays `plans`, `windows` and `cadence` through its door, and may replay `cadence_steps` through its feed bridge.",
  "constants": {
    "cursor_key_prefix": "vela.scanCursors.",
    "live_scan_blocks": 100,
    "backfill_lookback_secs": 604800,
    "backfill_max_blocks": 400000,
    "backfill_chunk_blocks": 10000,
    "backfill_chunks_per_poll": 4,
    "cadence_steps_ms": [15000, 30000, 60000, 120000],
    "cadence_hidden_ms": 120000,
    "cadence_interacting_max_ms": 60000,
    "cadence_scan_lost_ms": 300000
  },
